      "modernVersion": "NIV",
      "modernText": "The true light that gives light to everyone was coming into the world.",
      "meditation": "What does it mean to live in darkness? For some, it's the gray of depression—that fog where nothing seems meaningful or hopeful. For others, it's confusion—searching for meaning, purpose, truth. For some, darkness is the weight of loss, loneliness, or failure. But John says there is a true light. Not many lights, each illuminating the way you prefer. Not relative truth, each person finding their own way.\n\nOne true light. Jesus. And He came—into this world, to illuminate 「everyone.」 Without exception. Not just the smartest, the most virtuous, the most worthy. Every person born into this world. This includes you—in your darkest moments, in your confusion and failure. This true light isn't distant or untouchable.\n\nIt came into the world. It comes into your darkness. Light dispels darkness. Not through force or struggle, but simply by existing. You don't have to earn this light. You don't have to prove yourself worthy of it. You simply turn toward it.",
      "actionStep": "Today, if you're in darkness—even a little—turn toward the true light. Seek Jesus in your dark places and invite His light into your life.",
      "prayer": "Lord Jesus, you are the True Light that gives light to everyone—without exception, without barrier. Your light breaks through every darkness and reaches every corner of the world. Thank you that this light is available to all, shining equally on rich and poor, near and far. Amen."
