      "modernVersion": "NIV",
      "modernText": "Therefore go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit,",
      "meditation": "Go and make disciples of all nations. When you read those words, maybe doubt creeps in. Maybe you think you're not qualified, not knowledgeable enough, not spiritually mature enough. But hear what Jesus said just before: \"All authority in heaven and on earth has been given to me.\" This isn't saying you need to have all the answers.\n\nIt's saying: I have all the authority, and I'm going with you. Sharing faith doesn't require a divinity degree. It requires a real story. Maybe your friend is struggling at work, and you tell them how prayer helped you. Maybe someone is grieving, and your honesty about your own pain opens a conversation about hope.\n\nMaybe you're simply living differently—with more peace, more forgiveness, more joy—and someone asks why. Your voice matters. Your small witness, your genuine faith, your willingness to share what Jesus has done for you—that changes lives. You don't have to be an expert. You just have to be authentic.",
      "actionStep": "Think of one person in your life who seems spiritually open or searching. This week, initiate a genuine conversation with them. Don't force theology—just share one way your faith has helped you practically. Listen more than you talk. Plant a seed.",
      "prayer": "Lord Jesus, you commissioned us to go to all nations, baptizing in the name of the Father, Son, and Holy Spirit. What an awesome calling! Thank you for entrusting us with your mission and making us your witnesses to the world. You go before us and behind us, opening the way for your gospel to reach every corner of this earth. May our lives reflect the glory of your name — Father, Son, and Holy Spirit. Amen."
