      "modernVersion": "NIV",
      "modernText": "In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God.",
      "meditation": "Before light existed, before time began, there was the Word. Before galaxies, before atoms, before the first human breath—there was meaning. Purpose. Logic.\n\nThis opening is more than poetry; it's a claim about reality itself. When you navigate a chaotic world full of conflicting messages, you're searching for something solid. You're looking for meaning that won't crumble. This verse says that meaning has a name: Jesus.\n\nThe Word who was with God, who was God, who is God. Christ isn't an afterthought to creation or a reaction to human failure. He's the foundation of everything—the eternal logic that holds reality together. When you feel lost in meaninglessness, remember: you exist within a universe that was created by purpose and sustained by purpose. Your life matters because it's held by the eternal Word.",
      "actionStep": "Reflect on what gives your life meaning right now. Is it achievement, relationships, purpose? Now ask: would those things stand if Christ weren't at the center? Spend five minutes realigning your day with the truth that Christ is the anchor of meaning itself.",
      "prayer": "Lord, in the beginning was the Word, and that Word was with you and was you—eternal, divine, beyond all understanding. We stand in awe of this mystery and majesty. Thank you that the Word became flesh to dwell among us. Amen."
